# Purpose

This document defines how TypeScript is used throughout the hubIO platform.

Its purpose is to ensure the type system accurately represents business concepts, strengthens architectural boundaries, and enables safe evolution of the application as the platform grows.

---

# Scope

This standard defines:

* Type system philosophy
* Domain modeling
* Type ownership
* Type boundaries
* Runtime validation relationship
* Type governance

It intentionally excludes language syntax, framework-specific APIs, utility type implementation, and coding conventions, which are defined by their respective Engineering Standards.

---

# Constitutional Interpretation

This document extends the hubIO Engineering Constitution.

It applies constitutional engineering principles to the platform's type system, ensuring business rules are represented explicitly while maintaining long-term maintainability and architectural consistency.

